<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Surabaya</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1625 CE (approx.) · capital Surabaya</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The leading Muslim coastal state of East Java in the 16th and early 17th centuries, which resisted Sultan Agung of Mataram until 1625.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Surabaya, at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brantas-river">Brantas River</a>, grew as a Muslim port in the late 15th century as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> declined. Its rulers, styled adipati or duke, were allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/demak-sultanate">Demak</a> and after Demak's fall became the leaders of a league of East Javanese coastal states.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Surabaya controlled the trade of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brantas-river">Brantas</a> valley and the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java-sea">Java Sea</a>, with links to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banjarmasin">Banjarmasin</a>, Sukadana and the spice islands. Its rulers claimed descent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunan-ampel">Sunan Ampel</a>. At its height in the early 17th century it held influence over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gresik">Gresik</a>, Sedayu and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-agung">Sultan Agung of Mataram</a> conquered the coastal allies one by one and besieged Surabaya for years, finally damming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brantas-river">Brantas</a> to cut off its water. In 1625 Duke Jayalengkara surrendered. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pangeran-pekik">Pangeran Pekik</a> later served <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mataram-sultanate">Mataram</a> and married Agung's sister.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="duchy, 1500 CE – 1625 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="4